menu "Application (headset)"

    config HEADSET_ENABLE_USB
        bool "Enter USOUND at boot (starts the USB device stack)"
        default n
        help
            On the ESP32-S3 the USB-OTG PHY and the built-in USB-Serial/JTAG share
            D+/D-. Starting TinyUSB removes the USJ console until the board is
            re-plugged — and because this image re-takes the PHY about a second
            after every boot, replugging alone does not bring COM4 back: recovery
            is holding BOOT while replugging to reach ROM download mode.

            This is the whole point of the usound profile, so it must eventually be
            y. Leave it n while developing over USJ, and turn it on only with
            someone at the board or once TBD-009 (the UART console bridge) closes.

    config HEADSET_ENABLE_WIRELESS
        bool "Compile the wireless (wlink) profile and enter it when USB is not in use"
        default y
        help
            The Phase 2 profile: duplex audio to the dongle over subsys/audio_link
            (BLE 2M PHY + Opus, ADR-022). Unlike usound it leaves the
            USB-Serial/JTAG console alone, so an image with only this enabled is
            safe to flash remotely. Needs CONFIG_BT_ENABLED.

            With both profiles compiled, USB wins at boot and a long press of the
            action button switches between them.

    config HEADSET_WIRELESS_RETRY_S
        int "Re-enter WIRELESS from IDLE after (s)"
        default 30
        range 5 3600
        depends on HEADSET_ENABLE_WIRELESS
        help
            After the dongle has been gone longer than the profile's reconnect
            grace period the headset drops to IDLE, which releases the radio and the
            stream lock so the device may sleep. It advertises again after this
            long, or at once on a press of the action button.

    menu "Button pins"

        config HEADSET_BTN_PIN_VOL_DOWN
            int "Volume down"
            default 10

        config HEADSET_BTN_PIN_VOL_UP
            int "Volume up"
            default 11

        config HEADSET_BTN_PIN_ACTION
            int "Play/pause, and long-press mode override"
            default 0
            help
                Defaults to GPIO 0, the BOOT button, because it is the one control
                physically present on an S3 devkit and so the only one that can be
                exercised before the enclosure exists. It is RTC-capable, so it also
                serves as the deep-sleep wake source. The other two are placeholders.

    endmenu

    menu "Speaker (I2S TX) pins"

        config HEADSET_SPK_PIN_BCLK
            int "I2S BCLK"
            default 15

        config HEADSET_SPK_PIN_WS
            int "I2S WS / LRCLK"
            default 16

        config HEADSET_SPK_PIN_DOUT
            int "I2S DOUT"
            default 17

        config HEADSET_SPK_PIN_MCLK
            int "I2S MCLK (-1 if the DAC needs none)"
            default -1
            help
                Board wiring, shared by every profile that plays audio. Which DAC or
                amplifier part this is remains open (TBD-010), so these four pins
                are placeholders chosen not to collide with the microphone pins in
                applications/gunshot-aed. Set them for the real board before
                trusting a playback measurement.

    endmenu

    menu "Microphone (I2S RX) pins"

        config HEADSET_MIC_PDM
            bool "Microphone is PDM (else standard I2S)"
            default y

        config HEADSET_MIC_PIN_CLK
            int "PDM CLK or I2S BCLK"
            default 4

        config HEADSET_MIC_PIN_WS
            int "I2S WS (ignored for PDM)"
            default 5

        config HEADSET_MIC_PIN_DIN
            int "Data in"
            default 6
            help
                Same defaults as applications/gunshot-aed, and equally provisional:
                the microphone part is TBD-002. Shared by every profile.

    endmenu

endmenu
